                 Upstream bounds ir40 by iref as well; this core characterises
                 each count on its own. Levels are capped at 200 and the
                 half-step at 1000 units.

                 What is proved: each temperature level lies strictly between
                 the flux level above and the flux level below it, and is
                 exactly their midpoint; the level count within the structure
                 depth is the largest level whose flux depth does not exceed it;
                 the count at or above the sensor is the largest level whose
                 temperature depth does not exceed it. The two count theorems
                 are about integer division and are the ones that carry weight;
                 the midpoint and interleaving follow from the layout by
                 arithmetic on bounded operands.

